nts: o min: 20 o max: 2048 o pattern: arn:aws[a-z\-]*:iam::\d{12}:role/?[a-zA-Z_0-9+=,.@\-_/]+ BuiltInLifecycleConfigArn -&gt; (string) The lifecycle configuration that runs before the default lifecycle configuration. It can override changes made in the default lifecycle configuration. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 256 o pattern: (arn:aws[a-z\-]*:sage- maker:[a-z0-9\-]*:[0-9]{12}:studio-lifecycle-con- fig/.*|None) SpaceStorageSettings -&gt; (structure) The storage settings for a space. SageMaker applies these settings only to private spaces that the user creates in the domain. SageMaker doesn't apply these set- tings to shared spaces. DefaultEbsStorageSettings -&gt; (structure) The default EBS storage settings for a space. DefaultEbsVolumeSizeInGb -&gt; (integer) [required] The default size of the EBS storage volume for a space. Constraints: o min: 5 o max: 16384 MaximumEbsVolumeSizeInGb -&gt; (integer) [required] The maximum size of the EBS storage volume for a space. Constraints: o min: 5 o max: 16384 DefaultLandingUri -&gt; (string) The default experience that the user is directed to when access- ing the domain. The supported values are: o studio:: : Indicates that Studio is the default experience. This value can only be passed if StudioWebPortal is set to EN- ABLED . o app:JupyterServer: : Indicates that Studio Classic is the de- fault experience. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 1023 StudioWebPortal -&gt; (string) Whether the user can access Studio. If this value is set to DIS- ABLED , the user cannot access Studio, even if that is the de- fault experience for the domain. Possible values: o ENABLED o DISABLED CustomPosixUserConfig -&gt; (structure) Details about the POSIX identity that is used for file system operations. SageMaker applies these settings only to private spaces that the user creates in the domain. SageMaker doesn't apply these set- tings to shared spaces. Uid -&gt; (long) [required] The POSIX user ID. Constraints: o min: 10000 o max: 4000000 Gid -&gt; (long) [required] The POSIX group ID. Constraints: o min: 1001 o max: 4000000 CustomFileSystemConfigs -&gt; (list) The settings for assigning a custom file system to a user pro- file. Permitted users can access this file system in Amazon SageMaker AI Studio. SageMaker applies these settings only to private spaces that the user creates in the domain. SageMaker doesn't apply these set- tings to shared spaces. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 10 (tagged union structure) The settings for assigning a custom file system to a user profile or space for an Amazon SageMaker AI Domain. Permitted users can access this file system in Amazon SageMaker AI Stu- dio. NOTE: This is a Tagged Union structure. Only one of the follow- ing top level keys can be set: EFSFileSystemConfig, FSxLustreFileSystemConfig, S3FileSystemConfig. EFSFileSystemConfig -&gt; (structure) The settings for a custom Amazon EFS file system. FileSystemId -&gt; (string) [required] The ID of your Amazon EFS file system. Constraints: o min: 11 o max: 21 o pattern: (fs-[0-9a-f]{8,}) FileSystemPath -&gt; (string) The path to the file system directory that is accessi- ble in Amazon SageMaker AI Studio. Permitted users can access only this directory and below. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 256 o pattern: \/\S* FSxLustreFileSystemConfig -&gt; (structure) The settings for a custom Amazon FSx for Lustre file sys- tem. FileSystemId -&gt; (string) [required] The globally unique, 17-digit, ID of the file system, assigned by Amazon FSx for Lustre. Constraints: o min: 11 o max: 21 o pattern: (fs-[0-9a-f]{8,}) FileSystemPath -&gt; (string) The path to the file system directory that is accessi- ble in Amazon SageMaker Studio. Permitted users can access only this directory and below. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 256 o pattern: \/\S* S3FileSystemConfig -&gt; (structure) Configuration settings for a custom Amazon S3 file sys- tem. MountPath -&gt; (string) The file system path where the Amazon S3 storage loca- tion will be mounted within the Amazon SageMaker Stu- dio environment. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 1024 S3Uri -&gt; (string) [required] The Amazon S3 URI of the S3 file system configuration. Constraints: o min: 0 o max: 1024 o pattern: (s3)://([^/]+)/?(.*) StudioWebPortalSettings -&gt; (structure) Studio settings. If these settings are applied on a user level, they take priority over the settings applied on a domain level. HiddenMlTools -&gt; (list) The machine learning tools that are hidden from the Studio left navigation pane. (string) Possible values: o DataWrangler o FeatureStore o EmrClusters o AutoMl o Experiments o Training o ModelEvaluation o Pipelines o Models o JumpStart o InferenceRecommender o Endpoints o Projects o InferenceOptimization o PerformanceEvaluation o LakeraGuard o Comet o DeepchecksLLMEvaluation o Fiddler o HyperPodClusters o RunningInstances o Datasets o Evaluators HiddenAppTypes -&gt; (list) The Applications supported in Studio that are hidden from the Studio left navigation pane. (string) Possible values: o JupyterServer o KernelGateway o DetailedProfiler o TensorBoard o CodeEditor o JupyterLab o RStudioServerPro o RSessionGateway o Canvas HiddenInstanceTypes -&gt; (list) The instance types you are hiding from the Studio user inter- face. (string) Possible values: o system o ml.t3.micro o ml.t3.small o ml.t3.medium o ml.t3.large o ml.t3.xlarge o ml.t3.2xlarge o ml.m5.large o ml.m5.xlarge o ml.m5.2xlarge o ml.m5.4xlarge o ml.m5.8xlarge o ml.m5.12xlarge o ml.m5.16xlarge o ml.m5.24xlarge o ml.m5d.large o ml.m5d.xlarge o ml.m5d.2xlarge o ml.m5d.4xlarge o ml.m5d.8xlarge o ml.m5d.12xlarge o ml.m5d.16xlarge o ml.m5d.24xlarge o ml.c5.large o ml.c5.xlarge o ml.c5.2xlarge o ml.c5.4xlarge o ml.c5.9xlarge o ml.c5.12xlarge o ml.c5.18xlarge o ml.c5.24xlarge o ml.p3.2xlarge o ml.p3.8xlarge o ml.p3.16xlarge o ml.p3dn.24xlarge o ml.g4dn.xlarge o ml.g4dn.2xlarge o ml.g4dn.4xlarge o ml.g4dn.8xlarge o ml.g4dn.12xlarge o ml.g4dn.16xlarge o ml.r5.large o ml.r5.xlarge o ml.r5.2xlarge 